    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). \n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required that on a successful owner create, a welcome notification is enqueued by emitting \u2014 via the logger named `NOTIFY` \u2014 a line containing the owner id and the `memberId`.\n\nFollowing the OfficeFloor function-injection conventions in this repo, I made two changes:\n\n1. **New function class** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnqueueWelcomeNotification.java`. It takes the persisted `@Val Owner` and logs to `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"NOTIFY\")` a line carrying `owner.getId()` and `owner.getMemberId()`. It mirrors the style of the existing `AuditOwnerCreated` step (which logs to the `AUDIT` logger).\n\n2. **Wired it into the create pipeline** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`. Inserted a `notify` step between `audit` and `recordIdempotency`, keeping it under `govern: [ transaction ]` so the transaction span stays contiguous. Placing it after `save`/`audit` guarantees the generated owner id (and the assigned `memberId`) are populated.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` passes, and the full `./mvnw test` run is green. The captured log confirms the behaviour:\n\n```\nINFO  NOTIFY - Welcome notification enqueued: id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1\n```",
